.TH "HED-EXAMPLE" "1" "2026-08-22" "hed v1.21.2" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-example \- The starter template.
Copy this directory, rename, and you have a plugin.
.PP
The starter template.
Copy this directory, rename, and you have a plugin.
.SH Recipe
.IP
.EX
cp \-r plugins/example plugins/myplugin
cd plugins/myplugin
mv example.c myplugin.c
mv example.h myplugin.h
\f[I]# inside both files, replace \[ga]example\[ga] → \[ga]myplugin\[ga],\f[R]
\f[I]# \[ga]plugin_example\[ga] → \[ga]plugin_myplugin\[ga]\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Then in \f[CR]src/config.c\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\[dq]myplugin/myplugin.h\[dq]\f[R]
\&...
plugin_load(&plugin_myplugin, 1);
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]make\f[R] picks up the new \f[CR].c\f[R] automatically \[em] the
makefile globs \f[CR]*.c\f[R] recursively under \f[CR]plugins/\f[R].
.SH What the template demonstrates
.IP \[bu] 2
The minimum surface: an \f[CR]init\f[R] function and a \f[CR]Plugin\f[R]
descriptor.
.IP \[bu] 2
Registering a \f[CR]:\f[R] command (\f[CR]:hello\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
Registering a NORMAL\-mode keybind (\f[CR]<space>eh\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
Registering a hook (\f[CR]HOOK_MODE_CHANGE\f[R]).
.PP
That\[cq]s it.
Three patterns, \[ti]50 lines.
.SH Plugin contract
Every plugin exposes:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]typedef\f[R] \f[B]struct\f[R] Plugin {
    const char *name, *desc;
    int  (*init)(void);
    void (*deinit)(void);
} Plugin;

\f[B]extern\f[R] const Plugin plugin_myplugin;
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]plugin_load(&plugin_myplugin, 1)\f[R] registers the plugin and
runs its \f[CR]init()\f[R].
Pass \f[CR]0\f[R] to register without enabling \[em] useful for keymaps
that get swapped to at runtime via \f[CR]:keymap\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]init()\f[R] returns \f[CR]0\f[R] on success.
Inside it, register your commands with \f[CR]cmd(...)\f[R], your
keybinds with \f[CR]mapn(...)\f[R]/\f[CR]mapi(...)\f[R]/etc., and your
hooks with \f[CR]hook_register_*(...)\f[R].
All of those macros are in \f[CR]hed.h\f[R], which is the only include a
plugin should normally need.
.SH Out\-of\-tree plugins
Keep a plugin set outside the hed repo and point the build at it:
.IP
.EX
make PLUGINS_DIR=$HOME/my\-hed\-plugins
.EE
.PP
Headers from out\-of\-tree plugins are reachable as
\f[CR]#include \[dq]myplugin/myplugin.h\[dq]\f[R] because the makefile
passes \f[CR]\-I$(PLUGINS_DIR)\f[R].
.SH What \f[CR]init\f[R] should \f[I]not\f[R] do
.IP \[bu] 2
Don\[cq]t read configuration files at init time.
Plugins are loaded before \f[CR]main()\f[R] finishes setup; the file
system is fine but the rendering subsystem is not.
.IP \[bu] 2
Don\[cq]t print to stdout \[em] it goes to the terminal mid\-render.
Use \f[CR]log_msg(...)\f[R] (writes to the log file) or
\f[CR]ed_set_status_message(...)\f[R] (writes to the status line).
.IP \[bu] 2
Don\[cq]t keep the editor busy.
\f[CR]init()\f[R] is synchronous; if you need to do something heavy,
spawn a thread or defer to a hook (e.g., \f[CR]HOOK_STARTUP_DONE\f[R]).
